-- title:
--   Tower relations transfer to the degeneracy maps on function fields
-- statement:
--   The data of the statement fall into the following groups.
--
--   **Numerical data.** A nonzero squarefree level $N$, two distinct primes $q\neq q'$ (`hqq'`), neither dividing $N$ (`hqN`, `hq'N`), both at least $5$ (`hq5`, `hq'5`), and a nonzero natural number $D$ divisible by $2Nqq'$ (`hD`).
--
--   **The place above $q$.** A valuation subring $A_2$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `hA₂ : A₂.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A_2$; the decomposition subgroup of $A_2$ over $\mathbb Q$ acts by isometries for `A₂.valuation` (`hiso₂`); and a height-one prime $v_2$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $q$ (`hv₂`). The subfield [`ValuationSubring.ratClosure A₂`](def/ValuationSubring_CompletionRatClosure.html#L13) of the completion `A₂.valuation.Completion` is the topological closure of the prime subfield.
--
--   **The definite quaternion algebra and its orders.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef₁ : IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt q'`, that is $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$, the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q\in v$ is replaced by $q'\in v$. Two $\mathbb Z$-submodules $\Lambda_1\supseteq R_1$ (`hRΛ₁`) with $\Lambda_1$ a maximal order (`hΛ₁`) and $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$ (`hR₁`). A finite-idelic unit $n_1$ lying in `primeHeckeSet R₁ q` (`hn₁`), so that $n_1$ lies in the finite adelic box of $R_1$, $q\,n_1^{-1}$ lies in that box, while $n_1^{-1}$ and $q^{-1}n_1$ do not. The order `meetOrder R₁ n₁` $=R_1\cap R_1^{n_1}$ is required to be Eichler of level $Nq$ (`hS₁`), to be normalised by $n_1$ (`hnorm₁`), and the shift by $n_1$ on its class set is an involution (`hsq₁`). Finally `hlaws₁ : ClassSetHeckeLaws N q Λ₁ R₁ n₁` asserts four things: the edge Hecke matrices at all primes commute, the vertex Hecke matrices at all primes commute, for every prime $\ell\neq q$ and each of the two degeneracy maps the Hecke matrices intertwine the corresponding pushforward, and the common kernel of the two pushforwards is stable under every edge Hecke matrix.
--
--   **The indefinite quaternion algebra.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB : IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`, that is $0<a$ or $0<b$, and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly for the primes $v$ containing $q$ or $q'$; together with a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`).
--
--   **The curve over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and its moduli interpretation.** A field `Fbar` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is a curve function field in the sense of `IsCurveOver` (principal divisors of degree zero, residue fields finite over the base, $\Omega^1$ free of rank one) and essentially of finite type. A scheme $X$ with a morphism $\pi_X$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation of $\mathbb Z$ away from $D$, a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-point `sbar` of that base, and a family `pt` assigning to every commutative ring $S$, every $S$-point $s$ of the base and every false elliptic curve $E$ over $S$ (an abelian scheme of relative fibre dimension two with commutative group law, an action of $\Lambda$ subject to a trace condition, and level-$N$ data, `FakeEllipticCurve Λ N S`) a morphism to $X$ over $s$. The hypotheses `pt_iso`, `pt_pullback`, `pt_surjective`, `pt_injective` are the four coarse-moduli clauses for `pt`: invariance under isomorphism of false elliptic curves, compatibility with base change along ring maps, and surjectivity and injectivity up to isomorphism on points with values in algebraically closed fields. A curve model $\mathfrak M$ of `Fbar` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, an isomorphism $e_{\mathfrak M}$ from $\mathfrak M.C$ to the pullback of $\pi_X$ along `sbar` compatible with the structure morphisms (`he𝔐`), a Galois action `gal` by semilinear automorphisms of `Fbar`, a tower `𝕋 : HeckeTower.TowerData q q' Fbar` consisting of fields `𝕋.F ℓ` for the primes $\ell\neq q,q'$ together with finite integral $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra maps `𝕋.φ` from `Fbar`, Galois actions `galT` on the `𝕋.F ℓ`, involutions $W$ and `WT`, and a witness `tw : ModuliTowerWitnessD …` realising places of `Fbar` and of the `𝕋.F ℓ` by false elliptic curves over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with or without extra level structure, compatibly with `pt`, with the Galois and Atkin–Lehner actions and with both level-restriction maps.
--
--   **The $p$-adic uniformisation data on the definite side.** An injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_2$ from $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ to $2\times2$ matrices over `ratClosure A₂` (`hι₂`) and the induced projective representation $\rho_2$ into $\mathrm{PGL}_2$ (`hρ₂`); a pseudo-uniformiser $\varpi_2$ for `ratClosure A₂` inside the completion whose image is $q$ (`hϖ₂`), with `hdom₂` asserting that the ring of functions `Omega.HolRingOf ϖ₂ ρ₂` is a domain. Families $s_2$ of global units and `sf₂` of finite-idelic units indexed by the primes $\ell\neq q,q'$, subject to `hs₂`: for each $\ell$, the components of `sf₂ ℓ` away from $q$ are $s_2(\ell)\otimes1$, its components at the primes above $q$ are $1$, the product of the diagonal idele of the scalar $\ell$ with $(\mathrm{sf}_2\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_2\ell)=\ell$. Subgroups $\Gamma_2$ indexed by `HeckeTower.Obj q q'`, with `hΓ₂0` identifying $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$ with the units of `CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v₂` (units integral at every prime other than $v_2$) whose reduced norm has even $q$-adic valuation, and `hΓ₂ℓ` identifying $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{some}\ \ell)$ with the intersection of $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$ and its conjugate by $s_2(\ell)$. Elements $w_2$ and $\bar w_2$ with `hw₂` (reduced norm $q$ and integrality away from $v_2$ for $R_1$, respectively for `meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)`) and `hwbar₂` (reduced norm $q'$, local integrality at the primes other than $v_2$ not containing $q'$, and normalisation of the local boxes of $R_1$, of `meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)` and of $\Lambda_1$ at all primes other than $v_2$). A homomorphism `dIso₂` from the decomposition subgroup into isometric automorphisms of the completion realising the Galois action (`hdIso₂`). A quadratic character $\chi$ of the decomposition subgroup, trivial on inertia (`hχ₁`), nontrivial on every Frobenius element at $q$ (`hχ₂`), and whose kernel consists exactly of those $\tau$ fixing every $x$ in the residue field of $A_2$ with $x^{q^2}=x$ (`hχ₃`).
--
--   **Coefficient rings.** A characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O_0$ with irreducible element $\pi$, $\pi$-adically complete, with residue field of cardinality $q$, satisfying $(q)=(\pi)$, and having `ratClosure A₂` as fraction field, with $\pi$ mapping to $\varpi_2.\varpi$ (`hπϖ`), $N$ invertible in $\mathcal O_0$ (`hN₀`), and $\mathcal O_0$ cut out inside `ratClosure A₂` by the condition that the valuation be at most $1$ (`h𝒪₀`). An $\mathcal O_0$-algebra `Onr` which is a characteristic-zero domain, $\pi$-adically complete (`hOc`) with $(\pi)$ maximal (`hOm`), integral modulo $\pi$ (`hOa`) and with $\pi$-adic residue field algebraically closed in the sense that every monic polynomial of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOcl`), together with an $\mathcal O_0$-algebra automorphism `Fr` lifting the $q$-power map modulo $\pi$ (`hFr`). A homomorphism `vdet` from $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathrm{ratClosure}\ A_2)$ to $\mathbb Z$ measuring the $\pi$-valuation of the determinant up to units (`hvdet`), a ring map $\psi_0$ from `Onr` to the completion with values of valuation at most $1$ (`hψ₀`) extending the structure maps of $\mathcal O_0$ (`hψ₀𝒪`), and `hrk`, stating that for $x$ of valuation $<1$ and $y\neq0$ some power of the valuation of $x$ is at most that of $y$.
--
--   **Integral models, degeneracies and Atkin–Lehner maps.** A scheme $\mathcal X_0$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_0$ with structure morphism $f_0$ and points `pt₀` making it a coarse moduli space in the full sense of `IsCoarseModuli` (the four clauses above together with the universal property) (`h𝒳₀`), with $\mathcal X_0$ integral and $f_0$ flat, separated, locally of finite type and quasi-compact; for each prime $\ell\neq q,q'$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_0(\ell)$ over $\mathcal O_0$ with structure morphism $g_0(\ell)$ and points `ptT₀ ℓ` making it a coarse moduli space for false elliptic curves with extra level $\ell$ (`h𝒴₀`); two morphisms $d_{00}(\ell),d_{10}(\ell)$ to $\mathcal X_0$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) which on moduli points forget the extra level structure (`hd₀`) and pass to the target of a level-$\ell$ isogeny (`hd₁`); and endomorphisms `ar`, `arbar` of $\mathcal X_0$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising on moduli points the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $q$ and at $q'$ (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation.** Maps $\Theta$ and $\Theta_T(\ell)$ from the product of the functor corepresented by `Onr` with Drinfeld's functor `FormalOmega.Omega (ratClosure A₂) π` of Deligne data to the nilpotent points of $f_0$, respectively of $g_0(\ell)$, and a hypothesis `hCD` of twelve clauses, summarised here: naturality of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta_T(\ell)$; invariance of $\Theta$ under the twisted action of `CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v₂` and of $\Theta_T(\ell)$ under the twisted action of the intersection of that group with its conjugate by $s_2(\ell)$; for every algebraically closed $\mathcal O_0$-algebra with nilpotent $\pi$ and every $\mathcal O_0$-algebra map from `Onr`, surjectivity of $\Theta$, respectively $\Theta_T(\ell)$, in the Deligne-datum variable and the description of its fibres as orbits of the relevant twisted action; the universal property of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta_T(\ell)$ among such invariant natural families; the compatibility of $\Theta_T(\ell)$ with $d_{00}(\ell)$ and, after the twisted action of $s_2(\ell)$, with $d_{10}(\ell)$; and the compatibility of $\Theta$ with `ar` via the Frobenius twist by $1$ and with `arbar` via the twisted action of $\bar w_2(\mathrm{none})$.
--
--   **Base change to the completion.** The pullbacks of $f_0$ and of every $g_0(\ell)$ along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the composite $\mathcal O_0\to\mathrm{ratClosure}\ A_2\to A_2.\mathrm{valuation.Completion}$ are integral (`hXCint`, `hYCint`). An isomorphism $u$ between the pullback of $\pi_X$ along the completion point of the base and the pullback of $f_0$ along that composite, compatible with the second projections (`hu`) and with the moduli points `pt` and `pt₀` over the completion (`hupt`). A ring homomorphism $j$ from `Fbar` to the function field of the pullback of $f_0$, compatible with germs at generic points along the morphism obtained from $u^{-1}$, the canonical lift of the two projections and $e_{\mathfrak M}^{-1}$: whenever a section on an open $U\subseteq\mathfrak M.C$ containing the generic point has germ $\mathfrak M.\mathrm{ffEquiv}\,x$, its pullback has germ $j(x)$ at the generic point of the base-changed model (`hpin`).
--
--   **The fixed prime and the two legs.** A prime $\ell\neq q,q'$, with $g_0(\ell)$ locally of finite type and separated; two morphisms $dC_0,dC_1$ from the base-changed $\mathcal Y_0(\ell)$ to the base-changed $\mathcal X_0$ lifting $d_{00}(\ell)$ and $d_{10}(\ell)$ and commuting with both projections (`hdC₀`, `hdC₀'`, `hdC₁`, `hdC₁'`), both sending the generic point to the generic point (`hdom₀`, `hdom₁`); and two ring homomorphisms $\delta_0,\delta_1$ between the corresponding function fields which compute germs at the generic point along $dC_0$ and $dC_1$ respectively (`hδ₀`, `hδ₁`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every natural number $n$ and all families $x,y:\mathrm{Fin}\ n\to$ `Fbar`, if
--   $$\sum_{i} \mathbb T.\varphi(\ell,0)(x_i)\cdot \mathbb T.\varphi(\ell,1)(y_i)=0$$
--   in the field `𝕋.F ℓ`, then
--   $$\sum_{i} \delta_0(j(x_i))\cdot \delta_1(j(y_i))=0$$
--   in the function field of the pullback of $g_0(\ell)$ along the completion of $\mathcal O_0$. Thus the pair $(\delta_0\circ j,\ \delta_1\circ j)$ satisfies every bilinear relation over `Fbar` satisfied by the pair of degeneracy embeddings $\mathbb T.\varphi(\ell,0)$, $\mathbb T.\varphi(\ell,1)$.
--
--   This is the comparison step which transports the relations holding between the two degeneracy legs of the Hecke tower attached to `Fbar` to the corresponding pair of maps on the function fields of the Čerednik–Drinfeld integral models and their level-$\ell$ covers. It is the input needed to produce a ring homomorphism from `𝕋.F ℓ` to the function field of the level-$\ell$ model intertwining the two legs with $\delta_0$ and $\delta_1$, and is used for exactly that purpose by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_ringHom_functionField_level_germ_app_degeneracy_eq_of_germ_eq_of_iso_pullback_completion_zero_one_of_two_mul_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_ringHom_functionField_level_germ_app_degeneracy_eq_of_germ_eq_of_iso_pullback_completion_zero_one_of_two_mul_dvd). The proof combines the density of the locus of $\Omega$-points compatible with both degeneracy legs with the corresponding statement for curve models, [`AlgebraicCurve.CurveModel.sum_mul_eq_zero_of_sum_mul_eq_zero_of_dense_of_germ_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.CurveModel.sum_mul_eq_zero_of_sum_mul_eq_zero_of_dense_of_germ_eq).
